: [["**", -0.04314003139734268], [".**", -3.2383551597595215]]}, {"t": " (", "lp": -0.31320998072624207, "top": [[" (", -0.31320998072624207], [" unless", -1.9552502632141113]]}, {"t": "the", "lp": -0.1911499947309494, "top": [["the", -0.1911499947309494], ["default", -1.9267570972442627]]}, {"t": " default", "lp": -0.03984051197767258, "top": [[" default", -0.03984051197767258], [" driver", -3.4708364009857178]]}, {"t": ")", "lp": -0.6640594601631165, "top": [[")", -0.6640594601631165], [").", -0.7479541897773743]]}, {"t": " \u2014", "lp": -0.7117102146148682, "top": [[" \u2014", -0.7117102146148682], [" unless", -0.7708456516265869]]}, {"t": " you", "lp": -0.6392574906349182, "top": [[" you", -0.6392574906349182], [" it", -1.2299041748046875]]}, {"t": " likely", "lp": -0.41029730439186096, "top": [[" likely", -0.41029730439186096], [" rarely", -2.1658096313476562]]}, {"t": " don", "lp": -0.2270018756389618, "top": [[" don", -0.2270018756389618], [" won", -1.7965915203094482]]}, {"t": "'t", "lp": -0.0004147555155213922, "top": [["'t", -0.0004147555155213922], ["\u2019t", -8.823668479919434]]}, {"t": " need", "lp": -0.0008187664789147675, "top": [[" need", -0.0008187664789147675], [" even", -7.288986682891846]]}, {"t": " to", "lp": -0.0002722514618653804, "top": [[" to", -0.0002722514618653804], [" anything", -9.600744247436523]]}, {"t": " change", "lp": -0.0023418646305799484, "top": [[" change", -0.0023418646305799484], [" touch", -6.132596492767334]]}, {"t": " anything", "lp": -0.1192016452550888, "top": [[" anything", -0.1192016452550888], [" it", -2.268941879272461]]}, {"t": ".", "lp": -0.002937275217846036, "top": [[".", -0.002937275217846036], [" at", -6.561313629150391]]}, {"t": "\n", "lp": -0.0005052173510193825, "top": [["\n", -0.0005052173510193825], ["\n\n", -8.115884780883789]]}, {"t": "-", "lp": -0.00042525032768025994, "top": [["-", -0.00042525032768025994], [" ", -10.269449234008789]]}, {"t": " If", "lp": -1.7343010902404785, "top": [[" **", -1.0385174751281738], [" If", -1.7343010902404785]]}, {"t": " you", "lp": -0.0029486934654414654, "top": [[" you", -0.0029486934654414654], [" a", -7.101343154907227]]}, {"t": "'re", "lp": -0.1143045574426651, "top": [["'re", -0.1143045574426651], [" encounter", -2.3170957565307617]]}, {"t": " chasing", "lp": -0.5427768230438232, "top": [[" chasing", -0.5427768230438232], [" **", -2.0298430919647217]]}, {"t": " maximum", "lp": -1.2890506982803345, "top": [[" maximum", -1.2890506982803345], [" **", -1.562034249305725]]}, {"t": " performance", "lp": -0.0685562714934349, "top": [[" performance", -0.0685562714934349], [" benchmark", -4.096439838409424]]}, {"t": ",", "lp": -0.6986677646636963, "top": [[",", -0.6986677646636963], [" or", -1.3917028903961182]]}], "text": "# CCS Modes on Intel Arc (xe driver)\n\nThe `ccs_mode` parameter controls how **Compute and Copy Engines (CCS)** are assigned to hardware queues. This is set via the `xe` module parameter (e.g., `modprobe xe ccs_mode=2`).\n\n## The Modes\n\n**CCS Mode 1**\n- CCS engines are assigned to queues based on their **queue type/priority**.\n- Copy engines preferentially get dedicated CCS instances, while compute queues use different CCS assignments.\n- This is the more \"intelligent\" assignment that tries to match engine roles to CCS.\n\n**CCS Mode 2** *(the default)*\n- CCS engines are assigned to queues based on **queue index** (essentially a round-robin / index-based mapping).\n- This is the simpler, more predictable assignment and is generally the recommended default.\n- Works well for the vast majority of workloads.\n\n**CCS Mode 4**\n- Disables CCS assignment entirely \u2014 **all queues run on the primary/Engage (ENG) engine** without CCS delegation.\n- Effectively forces everything onto the main engine.\n\n## When to Use Which\n\n| Mode | Use case |\n|------|----------|\n| **2** | Default choice for most users. Best general performance/stability. |\n| **1** | Some users report different behavior with specific workloads; occasionally referenced in benchmarking scenarios. |\n| **4** | **Debugging or fallback** \u2014 use when you suspect CCS-related issues, want to isolate a problem to the primary engine, or are troubleshooting hardware/driver bugs. Not typically a performance choice. |\n\n## Practical Advice\n\n- **Start with mode 2** (the default) \u2014 you likely don't need to change anything.\n- If you're chasing maximum performance,"}